# Known False Positives for Pre-Push Scan
#
# Each entry describes a pattern the agent should recognize as a false
# positive when reviewing pre-push-scan.sh findings. The agent uses
# semantic matching — descriptions should explain the *reason* a finding
# is benign, not provide a grep pattern.
#
# Format: One description per bullet. Blank lines and comment lines
# (starting with #) are ignored.

- Username or SSH host alias matching against skill or knowledge
  description keywords in index files (e.g., model names like "granite"
  in skills/index.md coincidentally matching an SSH host alias)

- The literal placeholder `sk-litellm-local-no-auth` appearing in
  dsh-* and litellm-* skill files (SKILL.md, setup.sh,
  install-desktop.sh). The local LiteLLM proxy runs without a
  master_key and authenticates nothing; DSH only requires its
  apiKeyEnv variable to be non-empty. Not a credential. Lines
  matching the secrets pattern via `API_KEY=` are false positives.
